  "question": {
    "text": "Infinite number of masses, each 1 kg, are placed along the <math><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>16</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> ..... The magnitude of the resultant gravitational potential in terms of gravitational constant <math><mi>G</mi></math> at the origin <math><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is"
